# shared-types — Progress (Split 13 rewrite)

Tracks progress converting this package from Check! to Split 13. Tags reflect how much Split-13-specific work each file needs, not whether the current Check! code works.

Legend: [COMPLETE] no change needed · [IN PROGRESS] being worked on now · [NEEDS WORK] exists, must change/be replaced/repurposed · [MISSING] doesn't exist yet, needs to be created · [WARNING] works but flagged for review · [ERROR] known bug

Updated: 2026-08-30. Update this file in the same pass as any change to a listed file.

## Top-level config

- package.json — [NEEDS WORK] — name/description still say "Check!"; rename for Split 13.
- tsconfig.json — [COMPLETE]

## src/

- index.ts — [NEEDS WORK] — major: this is the whole client/server contract, and almost every shape in it is Check!-specific.
  - `GameStage`, `TurnPhase` — replace: Split 13 has no draw/discard/matching/ability phases, just deal → throw-loop → hand-over.
  - `PlayerStatus` — mostly replace: no `CALLED_CHECK`/`DISQUALIFIED` in Split 13; needs a bot-vs-human distinction instead.
  - `Card`, `Suit`, `CardRank`, `FacedownCard`/`PublicCard` — `Card`/`Suit`/`CardRank` reusable as-is (still a standard 52-card deck); `FacedownCard`/`PublicCard` are Check!-specific hidden-card plumbing that Split 13 likely doesn't need (no hidden hands) — confirm before keeping.
  - `Player`, `ClientCheckGameState` — full rewrite: no `pendingDrawnCard`, `publicPeek`/`publicSwap`/`publicPenalty`, `abilityStack`, `matchingOpportunity`, `discardPileIsSealed`/`discardTopIsLocked`; needs `team` (A/B), `isBot`, a single capture-stack shape, and per-team score fields instead of per-player.
  - `PlayerActionType` — full rewrite: collapses to essentially `THROW_CARD` plus lobby actions (start, ready, leave, seat/team pick) and bot-related actions if any are player-triggerable.
  - `ActiveAbility`, `AbilityType`, `Peek/Swap/SkipAbilityPayload`, `ClientAbilityContext` — [MISSING equivalent, not needed] — Split 13 has no special-card abilities; remove.
  - `SocketEventName`, `ServerToClientEvents`/`ClientToServerEvents` — mostly reusable shape (ack-based create/join/rejoin, broadcast state/log/chat); drop ability/peek-specific events (`ABILITY_PEEK_RESULT`, `INITIAL_PEEK_INFO`).
  - `RichGameLogMessage` — [COMPLETE] shape is generic; the `tags` union (`ability`, `penalty`, etc.) needs updating to Split 13's event vocabulary (e.g. `capture`).
  - `ChatMessage`, `BasicResponse`, `CreateGameResponse`/`JoinGameResponse`/`AttemptRejoinResponse`, `InitialPlayerSetupData`/`CreateGamePayload` — [COMPLETE] — generic lobby/chat plumbing, reusable as-is (CreateGamePayload's `maxPlayers?` becomes moot since Split 13 is fixed at 4, but harmless to leave optional).

## Planned / not yet created (Split 13-specific)

- `Team` enum/type (A/B) — [MISSING]
- `CaptureStack` type (replaces discard pile + matching-opportunity shapes) — [MISSING]
- Team score fields on the client game-state type — [MISSING]
- Bot-related types (e.g. `isBot` on `Player`, any bot-difficulty type if tiers are added later) — [MISSING]
